INSTALL


REQUIRED BUILD DEPENDENCIES

     on a debian system,
     apt install debhelper-compat libjpeg-dev libpng-dev libx11-dev libxext-dev libexif-dev libwebp-dev libtiff-dev pkgconf zlib1g-dev

     on other system in matter finding those include headers :
     libx11 with libxext
     libjpeg
     libpng
     libwebp
     libtiff
     libeexif
     zlib  gz, zip

     verify the command pkgconf or pkg-conf is around


    The JPEG reader assumes the IJG JPEG library is somewhere.
    get it from https://libjpeg.sourceforge.net/.

    The PNG reader assumes PNG group's library is installed.
    It's at http://www.libpng.org/  along with a
    lot of other PNG stuff.  libpng-1.0.5 or later is required.
    The PNG reader also require zlib installed.  https://www.zlib.net/


CONFIGURE

    There are a few compilation flags that one may need/want to change.
    This can be done in the Makefile file. The defines are:

	default is to use uncompress with .Z files
	-DHAVE_GUNZIP use gunzip rather than uncompress   .gz , .Z
	-HAVE_BUNZIP2 also use bunzip2  .bz2
	-DNO_UNCOMPRESS if the system doesn't have uncompress or gunzip.

    It maybe will matter changing some other variables to adapt to the system, as PKG_CONFIG, INSTALLDIR...


COMPILING

    The easiest way of compiling it is to use the Makefile. Simply
    run 'make', which should build xli.


INSTALL

    to try the results:
    ./xli   someimage

    copy the binary to final location
    cp xli  /usr/local/bin/


